            "paragraph": "The circulation over West Africa during the summer monsoon is dominated by the northward migration of the Inter-Tropical Front denoting the convergence between south-westerly monsoon winds and north-easterly dry Harmattan winds, and associated westward propagation of organised mesoscale convective systems linked to the position and strength of the African Easterly Jet (AEJ).\nfrom central Africa to the gulf of Guinea (West Africa) and the Atlantic Ocean in the mid-troposphere during July and August 2006 and suggested that it is driven by variations in the southern branch of the African Easterly Jet.",
